---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";
import Topbar from "../components/Topbar.astro";
import { SUBMIT_URL } from "../lib/themes.ts";
---
<Base
  title="Share a theme"
  description="Made a Spotifast theme you like? Share it here. Fill in one short form and it goes live on its own."
  current="submit"
>
  <header class="hero">
    <Topbar />
    <p class="eyebrow">Share a theme</p>
    <h1 class="big-title">Made something nice?</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Fill in one short form on GitHub. If everything checks out, your theme goes live in a few
      minutes. Nobody has to approve it by hand.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="main-inner prose">
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href={SUBMIT_URL} rel="noopener">
        <Icon name="plus" size={20} />Open the form
      </a>
    </div>

    <h2>What you'll need</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>A GitHub account.</li>
      <li>
        Your theme file. It's the same <code>.json</code> file you use in Spotifast, so just paste
        it in.
      </li>
      <li>A name for it, and a few tags if you want them.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>The theme file</h2>
    <p>
      It looks like this. <code>base</code> is <code>dark</code> or <code>light</code>, and any color
      you leave out comes from Spotifast's own theme.
    </p>
    <pre class="steps" style="overflow-x:auto;padding:20px"><code style="background:none;padding:0">{`{
  "base": "dark",
  "colors": {
    "window": "#121212",
    "accent": "#1ed760"
  }
}`}</code></pre>
    <p>
      Colors are written like <code>#1ed760</code>, or <code>#1ed76080</code> if you want some
      see-through. Keep the file under 4 KB. A full theme is usually around 700 bytes, so you've got
      lots of room.
    </p>

    <h2>Picking a name</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>3 to 30 characters, using letters, numbers and single spaces.</li>
      <li>It has to be new. Two themes can't share a name.</li>
      <li>
        Keep it friendly. Swear words, links, and names that sound official (like "Spotify" or
        "Admin") get turned away.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Making it readable</h2>
    <p>
      We check that people can actually read text in your theme. Here's what has to pass:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Main text on the background:</strong> at least 4.5 to 1 contrast.</li>
      <li><strong>Smaller text on the background:</strong> at least 3 to 1.</li>
      <li><strong>Text and icons on buttons:</strong> at least 3 to 1.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Not sure? Just send it. If something's off, the bot will tell you exactly which colors to
      change, and you can fix it by editing your form.
    </p>

    <h2>What happens next</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>A bot reads your form and checks your theme.</li>
      <li>If there's a problem, it leaves a comment saying what to fix.</li>
      <li>If it all looks good, your theme gets added and shows up here a few minutes later.</li>
      <li>
        Brand new GitHub accounts, and people sharing lots of themes in one day, wait for a person
        to take a look. That can take a while.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <h2>The fine print</h2>
    <p>
      Only share themes you made yourself. Everything here is released under
      <a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/" rel="noopener">CC0</a>, which means
      anyone can use, change, and share your theme for free.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
